IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr1-part1-payment`

-- Tests of cr1-part1-payment.l4 (Regulations 8 to 8.3). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text
-- (C.R.C.-c.-385.txt lines 138 to 192) and a calendar before the run. In 2026 these days fall on a Saturday:
-- 31 January, 7, 14, 21 and 28 February, 7, 14, 21 and 28 March, 4, 11, 18 and 25 April. 8 and 15 March are
-- Sundays, 3 April is a Friday.

§ `Tests of regulations 8 to 8.3`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN amwa2 IS A NUMBER
      amwa1 IS A NUMBER
      advised IS A BOOLEAN
      new IS A BOOLEAN
      onTime IS A BOOLEAN
      filed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cr1 Employer's withholding history`
`cr1 test history` amwa2 amwa1 advised new onTime filed MEANS `cr1 Employer's withholding history` WITH
    `average monthly withholding amount for the second calendar year preceding the particular calendar year` IS amwa2
    `average monthly withholding amount for the calendar year preceding the particular calendar year` IS amwa1
    `the employer has advised the Minister that the employer has elected` IS advised
    `the employer is a new employer throughout the particular month` IS new
    `throughout the 12-month period before that time the employer has remitted on time all the amounts required to be remitted` IS onTime
    `throughout the 12-month period before that time the employer has filed on time all the returns required to be filed` IS filed

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`cr1 test no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

§§ `Regulation 8(1): the 15th of the following month`

#ASSERT `reg 8(1) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 13) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 15)

§§ `Regulation 8(1.1)(a): the 25th, or the 10th of the following month`

-- Paid before the 16th day (up to and including the 15th): the 25th of the same month.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(a) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 25)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(a) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 25)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(a) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 12 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 12 25)
-- Paid after the 15th day: the 10th of the following month.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(a) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 16) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 10)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(a) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 10)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(a) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 12 16) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 10)

§§ `Regulation 8(1.1)(b): the third day, not counting a Saturday or holiday, after the part of the month`

#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — a day is a Saturday or a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 7) `cr1 test no holidays`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1.1)(b) — a day is a Saturday or a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 8) `cr1 test no holidays`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1.1)(b) — a day is a Saturday or a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 6) `cr1 test no holidays`)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — a day is a Saturday or a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 6) (LIST (YMD 2026 3 6))
-- The four parts of the month and their last days.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 7)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 7) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 7)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 8) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 14)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 14) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 14)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 21)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 21) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 21)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 22) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 3 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the last day of the period in which remuneration was paid` (YMD 2026 2 25) EQUALS (YMD 2026 2 28)
-- Paid 7 March: the period ends Saturday 7 March; 8 March (Sunday), 9 and 10 March are the first three days counted.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 7) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- If Sunday 8 March is also a holiday, 9, 10 and 11 March are counted.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 7) (LIST (YMD 2026 3 8)) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 11)
-- Paid 13 March: the period ends Saturday 14 March; 15 (Sunday), 16 and 17 March.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 17)
-- Paid 18 March: the period ends Saturday 21 March; 22 (Sunday), 23 and 24 March.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 18) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 24)
-- Paid 30 March: the period ends Tuesday 31 March; 1, 2 and 3 April.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 30) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 3)
-- With Friday 3 April a holiday: 1 and 2 April, then 3 April is skipped, Saturday 4 April is skipped, Sunday 5 April.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day by which contributions must be remitted` (YMD 2026 3 30) (LIST (YMD 2026 4 3)) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 5)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1)(b) — the day that is a number of counted days after a day` (YMD 2026 3 31) 0 `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 31)

§§ `Regulation 8(1.1) and (1.11): which way an employer remits`

-- The second preceding year's average monthly withholding amount: under $25,000, $25,000 to under $100,000, $100,000 or more.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1) — the way an employer shall remit` (`cr1 test history` 24999.99 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `remitting by the 15th day of the month following the month in which the remuneration was paid`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1) — the way an employer shall remit` (`cr1 test history` 25000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `remitting by the 25th day of the month, or the 10th day of the following month`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1) — the way an employer shall remit` (`cr1 test history` 99999.99 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `remitting by the 25th day of the month, or the 10th day of the following month`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.1) — the way an employer shall remit` (`cr1 test history` 100000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `remitting within three days, not counting a Saturday or holiday, after the end of the part of the month in which the remuneration was paid`
-- (1.11): the election, for an employer who would otherwise remit under (1.1)(a) or (b).
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 120000 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `remitting by the 15th day of the month following the month in which the remuneration was paid`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 50000 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `remitting by the 15th day of the month following the month in which the remuneration was paid`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 120000 25000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `remitting by the 25th day of the month, or the 10th day of the following month`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 120000 99999.99 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `remitting by the 25th day of the month, or the 10th day of the following month`
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 120000 100000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 120000 20000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No election where subsection (1) already applies: the employer would not "otherwise" remit under (1.1).
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.11) — the way an employer may elect to remit instead` (`cr1 test history` 20000 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 8(1.12) and (1.13): remitting quarterly`

-- (a) under $3,000 for either the first or the second preceding year; (b) remitted on time; (c) returns filed on time.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) — the employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 9000 2999.99 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) — the employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 2000 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1.12) — the employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 3000 3000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1.12) — the employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 2000 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1.12) — the employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 2000 2000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.13) — a new employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1.13) — a new employer may remit quarterly` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- The four quarterly days.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 1 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 3 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 9 30) EQUALS (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 10 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1.12) and (1.13) — the quarterly day for contributions paid in a month` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2027 1 15)

§§ `Regulation 8: the latest day to remit`

-- A small employer with no quarterly right: the 15th of the following month (paid 13 March, due 15 April).
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
-- $50,000: the 25th of the month (paid 13 March, due 25 March).
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 50000 50000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 25)
-- $120,000: three days after the part of the month (paid 13 March, due 17 March).
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 120000 120000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 17)
-- The same $120,000 employer who may elect (last year under $25,000, the Minister advised): 15 April.
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 120000 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
-- A new employer, otherwise on the 25th: the quarterly day, 15 April.
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 50000 50000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
-- A $120,000 employer whose last year was under $3,000 and who has paid and filed on time: quarterly, 15 April.
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 120000 2000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) (YMD 2026 3 13) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
-- Paid 1 July by a quarterly remitter: 15 October.
#ASSERT `reg 8 — the latest day by which contributions may be remitted` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2026 7 1) `cr1 test no holidays` EQUALS (YMD 2026 10 15)

§§ `Regulation 8(2): an employer who ceases to carry on the business`

#ASSERT `reg 8(2) — the day by which an employer who ceases to carry on a business must remit` (YMD 2026 6 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 17)
-- The earlier of seven days after ceasing and the day the other subsections give.
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) — the day by which contributions must be remitted, allowing for a cessation` (YMD 2026 7 15) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 17)
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) — the day by which contributions must be remitted, allowing for a cessation` (YMD 2026 4 15) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 10)) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) — the day by which contributions must be remitted, allowing for a cessation` (YMD 2026 4 15) NOTHING EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)

§§ `Regulation 8(1): on time`

#ASSERT `reg 8(1) — the contributions were remitted on time` (YMD 2026 4 15) (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) — the contributions were remitted on time` (YMD 2026 4 14) (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1) — the contributions were remitted on time` (YMD 2026 4 16) (YMD 2026 4 15))

§§ `Regulation 8(3): a return in prescribed form`

#ASSERT `reg 8(3) — the payment is accompanied by a return in prescribed form` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(3) — the payment is accompanied by a return in prescribed form` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(3) — the payment is accompanied by a return in prescribed form` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Regulation 8.1: the person deemed to be an employer`

#ASSERT `reg 8.1(1) — a person is deemed to be an employer of an employee` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.1(1) — a person is deemed to be an employer of an employee` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.1(1) — a person is deemed to be an employer of an employee` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 8.1(1.1) — the amount the person may recover from the actual employer` TRUE 1200 EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `reg 8.1(1.1) — the amount the person may recover from the actual employer` FALSE 1200 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8.1(2) — Part I of the Act applies to the person as if the actual employer` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.1(2) — Part I of the Act applies to the person as if the actual employer` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.1(2) — Part I of the Act applies to the person as if the actual employer` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 8.2: prescribed persons`

#ASSERT `reg 8.2(2) — the average monthly remittance` 6000000 12 EQUALS JUST 500000
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(2) — the average monthly remittance` 550000 11 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(2) — the average monthly remittance` 550000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1)(b) — the average monthly remittance is at least $50,000` (JUST 50000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1)(b) — the average monthly remittance is at least $50,000` (JUST 49999.99) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1)(b) — the average monthly remittance is at least $50,000` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a): an employer who must remit under (1.1)(b) (at least $100,000 for the second preceding year).
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1) — a person is a prescribed person` (`cr1 test history` 100000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1) — a person is a prescribed person` (`cr1 test history` 99999.99 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): acting for employers, average monthly remittance of at least $50,000 (600,000 over 12 months).
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1) — a person is a prescribed person` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE TRUE 600000 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1) — a person is a prescribed person` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE TRUE 599999.88 12 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1) — a person is a prescribed person` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE TRUE 600000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8.2(1) — a person is a prescribed person` (`cr1 test history` 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE 600000 12 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 8.3: the prescribed security interest`

#ASSERT `reg 8.3(1) — a mortgage is a prescribed security interest` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.3(1) — a mortgage is a prescribed security interest` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.3(1) — a mortgage is a prescribed security interest` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8.3(1) — a mortgage is a prescribed security interest` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (2): 500,000 outstanding less (300,000 other rights + 50,000 applied) = 150,000, for a failure after 1999.
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(2) — the most the prescribed security interest may be` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE 500000 300000 50000 EQUALS JUST 150000
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(2) — the most the prescribed security interest may be` (YMD 2010 6 30) TRUE 100000 80000 30000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(2) — the most the prescribed security interest may be` (YMD 1999 12 31) TRUE 500000 300000 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(2) — the most the prescribed security interest may be` (YMD 2010 6 30) FALSE 500000 300000 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(3) — an interest is included in a prescribed security interest` `insurance or expropriation proceeds relating to land or a building that is the subject of a registered mortgage interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(3) — an interest is included in a prescribed security interest` `a lien, a priority or any other security interest created by statute` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(3) — an interest is included in a prescribed security interest` `an assignment or hypothec of rents or of leases` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(3) — an interest is included in a prescribed security interest` `a mortgage interest in equipment or fixtures that a mortgagee or another has the right to remove or dispose of separately from the land or building` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8.3(3) — an interest is included in a prescribed security interest` `another interest` EQUALS NOTHING
